WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:16.022
After dinner Daisy met Kaleem outside.

2
00:00:16.023 --> 00:00:18.069
They were going to wait for dusk.

3
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:21.041
Bats were nocturnal.

4
00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:25.457
So that was when they were most likely to appear.

5
00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:29.454
"Psst, Daisy!" Beatrice buzzed over.

6
00:00:29.455 --> 00:00:32.791
"Did you think of an animal to study yet?"

7
00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:35.374
"Nope," Daisy said.

8
00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:39.973
She laughed as she told Kaleem what Beatrice had just said.

9
00:00:39.974 --> 00:00:42.730
"Beatrice wants me to choose an animal fast.

10
00:00:42.731 --> 00:00:45.582
She seems almost worried about me."

11
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:49.744
Kaleem grinned. "Maybe she's excited about the project too.

12
00:00:49.745 --> 00:00:54.477
Hey, we can think about your animal while we wait for the sun to set."

13
00:00:54.478 --> 00:00:57.816
Daisy nodded. "Great idea.

14
00:00:57.817 --> 00:01:01.301
There are lots of animals near the edge of the woods in your yard.

15
00:01:01.302 --> 00:01:12.163
Let's hang out there. I might get inspired."

16
00:01:12.164 --> 00:01:16.475
Sure enough, a pretty red cardinal landed on a tree.

17
00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:22.791
"Hey, Daisy. Can you tell your dad to fill the bird feeder? We need more seeds."

18
00:01:22.792 --> 00:01:29.366
"Sure. By the way . . ." Daisy told the bird about her project.

19
00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:32.459
He cocked his head. "You could study me!

20
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.514
My red feathers would make a great photo."

21
00:01:35.515 --> 00:01:40.877
Daisy smiled. "That's true. But another student picked cardinals."

22
00:01:40.878 --> 00:01:47.707
"Ask him if he's seen any bats," Kaleem said.

23
00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:51.082
"Bats come out only when it's dark," the cardinal said.

24
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:54.535
"And I fly only during the day.

25
00:01:54.536 --> 00:02:02.653
That reminds me—it's getting late. Good night!"

26
00:02:02.654 --> 00:02:11.124
After the cardinal flew away, Daisy talked to a skunk and then a toad.

27
00:02:11.125 --> 00:02:14.334
They hadn't seen any bats lately.

28
00:02:14.335 --> 00:02:19.520
Neither had the deer peeking out from the woods.

29
00:02:19.521 --> 00:02:24.108
Daisy shrugged. "Maybe bats don't live around here.

30
00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:28.605
I've never talked to one. I've never even seen one."

31
00:02:28.606 --> 00:02:33.227
"I have," Kaleem said. "I remember watching them when I was younger.

32
00:02:33.228 --> 00:02:37.405
It probably just isn't late enough." He sighed.

33
00:02:37.406 --> 00:02:42.582
"It might be tricky to get a picture of a bat. I can't stay up all night."

34
00:02:42.583 --> 00:02:48.867
"We can keep trying," Daisy said.

35
00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:53.457
"Let's ask our parents if we can sit by my firepit tomorrow night.

36
00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:57.480
I bet they'll let us stay out later than usual because of the project."

37
00:02:57.481 --> 00:03:03.624
"Great idea!" Kaleem said.

38
00:03:03.625 --> 00:03:11.582
Daisy gently set Beatrice on a bush to sleep.

39
00:03:11.583 --> 00:03:15.668
Then she said good night to Kaleem and headed home.

40
00:03:15.669 --> 00:03:18.265
It was getting dark.

41
00:03:18.266 --> 00:03:30.332
But the streetlights had blinked on, and so had the light above her back door.

42
00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:37.254
As she reached it, she saw moths, mosquitoes, and other bugs swarming around it.

43
00:03:37.255 --> 00:03:40.014
"Shoo! Out of my way, please!"

44
00:03:40.015 --> 00:03:47.916
By waving her hand gently, Daisy made it inside, keeping the insects outside.

45
00:03:47.917 --> 00:03:52.332
"Daisy, there you are," her mom said.

46
00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:56.324
"Kaleem and I were watching for bats."

47
00:03:56.325 --> 00:04:00.561
Daisy told her parents about the school project.

48
00:04:00.562 --> 00:04:04.053
"We used to see lots of bats around here," her dad said.

49
00:04:04.054 --> 00:04:07.166
"They would arrive nearly every day at dusk."

50
00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:11.291
Mom nodded. "There were so many of them!

51
00:04:11.292 --> 00:04:17.043
My grandma used to joke that they'd get tangled in her hair."

52
00:04:17.044 --> 00:04:19.103
She looked out a window.

53
00:04:19.104 --> 00:04:23.431
"Now that you mention it, I haven't spotted a bat in a long time."

54
00:04:23.432 --> 00:04:28.438
"Well . . ." Daisy felt worried and curious at the same time.

55
00:04:28.439 --> 00:04:35.563
"I'm going to figure out where they went!"

